## You found the gap. Now improve the food.

Once a repeated gap appears, the next step should be practical.

Nutrient density means choosing foods that provide a high amount of useful nutrition without needing to radically increase food volume or complexity.

Useful foods may include, according to preference and tolerance:

- eggs;
- sardines;
- oily fish;
- quality dairy;
- legumes;
- nuts;
- seeds;
- colourful vegetables;
- fruit;
- shellfish or other zinc-rich foods;
- mineral-rich whole foods.

## The food-first logic

```text
IDENTIFY GAP
↓
CHOOSE A USEFUL FOOD
↓
REPEAT CONSISTENTLY
↓
REVIEW RESPONSE
```

Examples:

### Eggs
Can contribute:
